-- check/bad: a dot-call on a record field is still a field call (§1.2), and
-- an argument mistake underlines THAT ARGUMENT — `"two"` at 13:25 — and
-- names the field, exactly as the `call(field_access(…))` this replaced
-- did. A regression guard for the whole argument path of a `method_call`,
-- including `Solve.argRegions`, which had no arm for the new tag: the
-- arguments of a method call are a range inside its payload and not `rhs`
-- itself, so the fallback would have underlined the whole call.
pub type alias Adder =
    add : Int, Int -> Int


pub sum : Adder -> Int
sum adder = adder.add 1 "two"
